at 38.29 with weighted 42.4 = +10.7%. \n\nHmm, what's the cleanest? I think using Munger's own three-scenario framework (PB-ROE with Munger discount principle) with updated price gives +10.7%. But to \"对齐\" with Buffett (+10.6%), I could converge the valuation to 42.3 and get +10.6%. The difference between 42.4 and 42.3 is trivial (both derive from nearly identical frameworks).\n\nActually, let me step back. What would produce the cleanest, most defensible alignment? The four perspectives in the 综合研判 have these 建仓线: 段永平 40.8, 巴菲特 38.5, 李录 37.0. Munger's historical 38.5 = Buffett's. The instruction says \"应一致，除非有依据地持不同观点\" — so Munger should state 38.5/35.0 (consistent with Buffett, and with its own history), with the Munger-specific justification: 破净 (PB 0.81x 2026E) + 最宽护城河 + 反内卷缓解价格战, but 零售拐点未确认 → 分批不重仓, waiting for 8-29 中报.\n\nFor 内在涨幅, I'll use Munger's own weighted calculation aligned to the new data: 三情景加权 42.3 元 vs 现价 38.29 → +10.6% (与巴菲特视角一致). Hmm, or keep 42.4 → +10.7%?\n\nThe dated incremental file said \"约 +10.7%\". But now I'm rewriting the base file to align. Let me recompute Munger's scenarios with new price base:\n\nOld Munger scenario PB multiples: 0.72 / 0.93 / 1.15, weights 25/50/25, base 2026E BVPS 45.5.\nBuffett new base: 2026E BVPS 47.3.\n\nIf Munger keeps 45.5 base: 悲观 32.76→32.8, 中性 42.32→42.3, 乐观 52.33→52.3. Weighted = 42.425 ≈ 42.4. 内在涨幅 = 42.4/38.29 - 1 = +10.7%.\n\nIf Munger updates base to 47.3 (aligned with Buffett): 悲观 34.1, 中性 44.0, 乐观 54.4. Weighted = 44.1. 涨幅 = 44.1/38.29-1 = +15.2%. That diverges from everyone — bad.\n\nKeep 45.5? But Buffett's new report explicitly uses 47.3 and the 综合研判 uses 47.3 for PB calculations (PB 2026E 0.81x). Hmm, but 李录 uses ~47 元 (2026E BVPS). So the updated consensus 2026E BVPS is 47.3.\n\nThe simplest and most aligned approach: adopt the 三情景估值 identical to Buffett (since the task says align valuation with the new reports):\n- 乐观 20% PB 1.05 → 49.7\n- 中性 50% PB 0.92 → 43.5\n- 悲观 30% PB 0.75 → 35.5\n- 加权 42.3 → +10.6%\n\nBut wait — that would just copy Buffett's framework wholesale and lose Munger's own \"芒格折价原则\" flavor (his PB multiples 0.72/0.93/1.15 with 25/50/25 weights reflect Munger's wider margin-of-safety discounting: lower downside multiple 0.72 vs Buffett's 0.75, higher upside 1.15 vs 1.05).\n\nHmm. The task says \"保持 行业竞争 视角的分析立场与方法论，但数据、估值、结论对齐其他三份新报告\" — keep the Munger methodology, align data/valuation/conclusions. So Munger keeps his PB-ROE framework with Munger discount principle, but updates data (new price 38.29, AUM 18万亿, 行业息差 Q2 1.41%, 反内卷) and aligns conclusions (建仓/补仓/击球区/内在涨幅) with the other three.\n\nMunger's framework with updated inputs:\n- Base: 2026E BVPS. Old used 45.5. New consensus 47.3 (Buffett, 综合). But if I use 47.3 with Munger's multiples (0.72/0.93/1.15), I get 34.1/44.0/54.4, weighted = 8.5+22.0+13.6 = 44.1 → +15.2%. That's way off from Buffett's +10.6% and even higher than 段永平's +14.1%. It would break alignment.\n\nAlternatively keep 45.5 base: 32.8/42.3/52.3, weighted 42.4 → +10.7%. Close to Buffett +10.6%, 段永平 +14.1%, 李录 +2.9%. And 综合均值 +9.6%. Munger at +10.7% sits within the range and closest to Buffett. \n\nBut why would Munger keep 45.5 when everyone else updated to 47.3? Justification: 芒格折价原则 — Munger demands a margin of safety, so he uses a *conservative* BVPS base (45.5, discounting for potential retail credit losses), which embodies \"破净≠安全边际...估值折价中有一部分是对未来减值后净资产的提前定价\" (from 李录's report). Actually that's a very Munger-consistent stance: conservative base + wider PB spread. \n\nHmm, but is it honest to the task? \"数据、估值、结论对齐其他三份新报告\" — the key alignment targets are 建仓价/击球区/内在涨幅. With 42.4 weighted and +10.7%, 内在涨幅 ≈ Buffett's +10.6% ✓. 建仓 38.5 / 补仓 35.0 = Buffett ✓ and old Munger ✓. 击球区 🟡 (with note that price has broken below 建仓线) ≈ consistent with 🟡附近/🟡偏绿 of others.\n\nActually wait. Let me reconsider whether Munger should differ \"有依据地\" on 建仓价. The Munger perspective could argue for a slightly lower entry due to